build/
build-*/
data/*
!data/README.md
*.cphd
*.cphd.truth
*.f32
*.png
*.pgm
*.csv

# Run outputs ARE the record and belong in git, so runs/ opts back in.
#
# The rules above exist to keep collects and stray scratch images out of the
# repository, and they were catching the figures and per-window evidence too --
# which is how a finished run came to be undocumented except by its reported
# number. A run directory is kilobytes to a few megabytes; that is worth
# keeping. Raw cubes are not: .f32 stays ignored everywhere because it is
# regenerable from the CSV and the commit, and *.cphd stays ignored because a
# collect is referenced by vendor name, never committed.
!runs/**/*.png
!runs/**/*.csv
!runs/**/*.log
!runs/**/*.md
